From: Alan Shearer <alan@localhost>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 09:15:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] virtio_block: delete DMAResource and IOScheduler in uninit_driver

DMAResource is allocated in virtio_block_init_driver. IOScheduler is
allocated later in virtio_block_set_capacity (called from init_device
after a successful config read). Both are only deleted in
virtio_block_uninit_device.

uninit_device runs only if init_device set *_cookie. That assignment
is after read_device_config and alloc_queues, so those early returns
never call uninit_device. register_child_devices failing after
init_driver (create_id / publish_device) is the same: teardown is
uninit_driver only. alloc_queues failing after set_capacity also
leaves IOScheduler allocated.

Delete both objects from uninit_driver as a fallback. NULL the
pointers in uninit_device so a later uninit_driver on the success
unload path is not a double-delete.

---
 src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/disk/virtual/virtio_block/virtio_block.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/disk/virtual/virtio_block/virtio_block.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/disk/virtual/virtio_block/virtio_block.cpp
index 9eb71254daec..b1c0d0d0d0d0 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/disk/virtual/virtio_block/virtio_block.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/disk/virtual/virtio_block/virtio_block.cpp
@@ -318,7 +318,9 @@ virtio_block_uninit_device(void* _cookie)
 	virtio_block_driver_info* info = (virtio_block_driver_info*)_cookie;
 
 	delete info->io_scheduler;
+	info->io_scheduler = NULL;
 	delete info->dma_resource;
+	info->dma_resource = NULL;
 }
 
 
@@ -599,6 +601,10 @@ virtio_block_uninit_driver(void *_cookie)
 	CALLED();
 	virtio_block_driver_info* info = (virtio_block_driver_info*)_cookie;
 	mutex_destroy(&info->lock);
+	delete info->io_scheduler;
+	info->io_scheduler = NULL;
+	delete info->dma_resource;
+	info->dma_resource = NULL;
 	delete_area(info->bufferArea);
 	free(info);
 }
